# The run of pme-settle.test on a GPU, over 0.5 ps: in double precision it
# gives the energies of the CPU to the digits of the log, and in mixed
# precision it conserves the energy as well. In the deterministic mode the
# charges are spread in fixed point, so a run on the device gives the same
# state from run to run, to the bit (D84); by default they are added with
# floating-point atomics. With the reciprocal sums on a second stream
# (md-exec-assign-streams, D87), the state is the same to the bit again:
# evidence, beside the argument of D87, that the ops that run beside them
# are independent of them.
#
# REQUIRES: cuda, hdf5
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: cp %S/Inputs/opc/opc.prmtop %S/Inputs/opc/opc.inpcrd %t
# RUN: sed -n '/^#--- run.toml/,/^#--- end/p' %S/pme-settle.test | sed '1d;$d' \
# RUN:     | sed -e 's|^steps *= 100|steps = 500|' -e 's|energy_interval = 50|energy_interval = 500|' > %t/run.toml
# RUN: sed -e 's|^type = "PERIODIC"|type = "PERIODIC"\n[execution]\ntarget = "gpu"\ndeterministic = true|' %t/run.toml > %t/double.toml
# RUN: sed -e 's|^energy_interval = 500|energy_interval = 500\ncheckpoint = "first.h5"\ncheckpoint_interval = 500|' %t/double.toml > %t/first.toml
# RUN: sed -e 's|^energy_interval = 500|energy_interval = 500\ncheckpoint = "second.h5"\ncheckpoint_interval = 500|' %t/double.toml > %t/second.toml
# RUN: sed -e 's|^energy_interval = 500|energy_interval = 500\ncheckpoint = "side.h5"\ncheckpoint_interval = 500|' %t/double.toml > %t/side.toml
# RUN: sed -e 's|^type = "PERIODIC"|type = "PERIODIC"\n[execution]\ntarget = "gpu"\nprecision = "mixed"|' %t/run.toml > %t/mixed.toml
# RUN: cd %t && mdir run first.toml > first.log
# RUN: cd %t && mdir run second.toml > second.log
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DOUBLE < %t/first.log
# RUN: mdir checkpoint %t/first.h5 %t/second.h5 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SAME
# RUN: cd %t && mdir emit side.toml --stage=pipeline \
# RUN:     | sed 's|md-exec-assign-streams,|md-exec-assign-streams{reciprocal=true},|' > pipeline
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_PRINT_AFTER=md-exec-assign-streams sh -c 'MDIR_PIPELINE="$(cat pipeline)" mdir run side.toml' > side.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SIDE < %t/side.log
# RUN: mdir checkpoint %t/first.h5 %t/side.h5 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SAME
# A run of one step with no energies: the scratch of the reciprocal sum is
# allocated after the test of the neighbor structure, so the sum stays
# after the test rather than going before it (D113).
# RUN: sed -e 's|^steps = 500|steps = 1|' -e 's|^energy_interval = 500|energy_interval = 0\ncheckpoint = "one.h5"\ncheckpoint_interval = 1|' %t/mixed.toml > %t/one.toml
# RUN: cd %t && mdir run one.toml | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ONE
# RUN: mdir run %t/mixed.toml | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MIXED

# SAME: the states are identical
# SIDE: md_exec.reciprocal {{.*}} {md_exec.side}
# SIDE: md_exec.join
# DOUBLE: INFO:       500         0.5000 {{ *}}-2811.6418 {{ *}}-3754.0060 {{ *}}942.3642
# DOUBLE: MDIR: the total energy changed by {{[0-9.]+}}e-0{{[5-9]}} of its value
# MIXED:  MDIR: the total energy changed by {{[0-9.]+}}e-0{{[5-9]}} of its value

# ONE: MDIR: the total energy changed by
